# Arguments the deltahedger service runs with.
#   sudo systemctl restart deltahedger    # after any change here
#
# It ships in --dry-run: every decision is computed and logged, no order is
# placed. Run it that way for at least one full session and read the journal
# before you take the flag off. A dry run exercises the whole path except
# the fill, so it is the cheapest way to find out that market data is
# missing, or that the regime never leaves neutral, or that the entry window
# is wrong for how your day actually looks.
#
# When you are ready to route to the PAPER account, delete --dry-run:
#
#   DELTAHEDGER_ARGS=live -c configs/es_paper.yaml
#
# cli.py refuses to route ANY non-dry-run order -- paper included -- unless
# ibkr.allow_live_trading is true in the config, so es_paper.yaml already
# sets it. That flag also happens to be what gates connecting to a
# non-paper account; the account actually used is decided by which account
# the Gateway session is logged into (TradingMode in /etc/ibc/config.ini),
# not by this file.

DELTAHEDGER_ARGS=live -c configs/es_paper.yaml --dry-run
